WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:03.230
- This week, we're coming
to you from the past!

00:00:03.230 --> 00:00:06.310
- Chuck, everything we
experience through our senses

00:00:06.310 --> 00:00:07.620
has happened in the past.

00:00:07.620 --> 00:00:10.940
'Cause we see things not as
they are but as they once were

00:00:10.940 --> 00:00:13.310
because of the light
travel time between us.

00:00:13.310 --> 00:00:16.780
- That's awful, especially
when you consider my past.

00:00:16.780 --> 00:00:19.410
- I don't wanna know
your past, all I know is

00:00:19.410 --> 00:00:21.425
this is wheel of science.

00:00:21.425 --> 00:00:24.508
(upbeat theme music)

00:00:26.390 --> 00:00:28.720
- Hey everybody, Welcome
to Wheel of Science.

00:00:28.720 --> 00:00:30.013
- The interactive show where we answer

00:00:30.013 --> 00:00:32.430
your questions about the universe.

00:00:32.430 --> 00:00:34.482
I'm your host Chuck Nice and
I don't answer your questions.

00:00:34.482 --> 00:00:38.090
We have with us as
usual the one, the only,

00:00:38.090 --> 00:00:42.410
Doctor Neil deGrasse
Tyson, what's up Neil?

00:00:42.410 --> 00:00:43.298
You know I love doin' that.

00:00:43.298 --> 00:00:45.490
So Neil, you're beaming in from Vegas huh?

00:00:45.490 --> 00:00:47.839
- Yeah I got a gig tonight,
I'm giving a public talk

00:00:47.839 --> 00:00:49.530
on Astrophysics.

00:00:49.530 --> 00:00:51.830
There is some learning that
goes on in the town apparently.

00:00:51.830 --> 00:00:53.640
- I was gonna say, that's
the most exciting thing

00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:56.270
I've ever heard happening in Vegas.

00:00:56.270 --> 00:00:57.130
Well one thing is for sure,

00:00:57.130 --> 00:00:59.540
We know we always win when we
bet on Neil deGrasse Tyson.

00:00:59.540 --> 00:01:02.490
- You're really betting on the
universe when you bet on me,

00:01:02.490 --> 00:01:05.230
'cause all I am is a conduit to it.

00:01:05.230 --> 00:01:07.123
- Oh, I meant bet on the black.

00:01:08.030 --> 00:01:10.801
Anyway, so Neil what time is it my friend?

00:01:10.801 --> 00:01:12.350
- Just spin the wheel.

00:01:12.350 --> 00:01:13.602
- There you go.

00:01:13.602 --> 00:01:16.352
(spinning noise)

00:01:17.522 --> 00:01:19.594
- [Chuck] Annaliisa Essi Katriina Lee says

00:01:19.594 --> 00:01:22.122
my daughters, ages eight
and eleven, want to know

00:01:22.122 --> 00:01:25.573
Would it actually be easier
to travel forward in time

00:01:25.573 --> 00:01:29.360
rather than backward and
what would that require?

00:01:29.360 --> 00:01:31.663
- Oh we can easily travel forward in time

00:01:31.663 --> 00:01:35.430
and we've known how to do that since 1905.

00:01:35.430 --> 00:01:37.740
Einsteins special theory of relativity

00:01:37.740 --> 00:01:39.199
lays out the whole recipe

00:01:39.199 --> 00:01:41.670
of how you can move into the future.

00:01:41.670 --> 00:01:44.800
And all you have to do
is go into a sort of a

00:01:44.800 --> 00:01:47.940
lower gravity field
relative to other people.

00:01:47.940 --> 00:01:51.930
Or just travel very fast and
your clock will tick slower

00:01:51.930 --> 00:01:55.020
than that of everybody
else that you left behind.

00:01:55.020 --> 00:01:58.020
Then when you return, you'll
be younger than your twin

00:01:58.020 --> 00:02:01.140
for example, if you had left
your twin back on earth.

00:02:01.140 --> 00:02:04.040
So, in that sense you are
traveling into the future.

00:02:04.040 --> 00:02:06.671
That's easy to do, and
we've known how to do that.

00:02:06.671 --> 00:02:10.600
Traveling backwards, that's the problem.

00:02:10.600 --> 00:02:12.910
And it takes, we think we can do that.

00:02:12.910 --> 00:02:15.700
I have some colleagues
who've made some calculations

00:02:15.700 --> 00:02:16.960
that ...

00:02:16.960 --> 00:02:19.670
assert that depending on a

00:02:19.670 --> 00:02:22.793
trajectory intake around a
black hole you can come out

00:02:22.793 --> 00:02:25.853
and end up in the past
of when you started.

00:02:25.853 --> 00:02:27.151
So ...

00:02:27.151 --> 00:02:29.640
but that takes extraordinary set up

00:02:29.640 --> 00:02:30.479
to make happen.

00:02:30.479 --> 00:02:33.650
But right now, no problem
traveling into the future.

00:02:33.650 --> 00:02:36.912
- So, its either lower
gravity, travel faster than

00:02:36.912 --> 00:02:39.832
the speed of light, or
very good moisturizer.

00:02:39.832 --> 00:02:42.582
(Neil chuckling)

00:02:43.512 --> 00:02:46.360
- Not only that, the GPS satellites,

00:02:46.360 --> 00:02:47.691
which are farther away from the center

00:02:47.691 --> 00:02:49.570
of the earth than we are.

00:02:49.570 --> 00:02:52.260
They experience less gravity than we do.

00:02:52.260 --> 00:02:56.000
The GPS clocks tick
faster than our clocks,

00:02:56.000 --> 00:02:58.750
yet we're getting our time from them.

00:02:58.750 --> 00:03:01.610
And so they know this in advance, rather.

00:03:01.610 --> 00:03:06.240
We've programmed in the
relativity correction

00:03:06.240 --> 00:03:09.430
to compensate for this
fact, So when they do

00:03:09.430 --> 00:03:10.872
give us the time, it's the right time

00:03:10.872 --> 00:03:14.570
not the relativistic time
that it wants to keep

00:03:14.570 --> 00:03:16.430
by being where it is in orbit.

00:03:16.430 --> 00:03:17.263
Awesome!

00:03:17.263 --> 00:03:18.900
- Alright Neil, you ready
for the next question?

00:03:18.900 --> 00:03:20.373
- Spin the wheel!

00:03:20.373 --> 00:03:23.123
(spinning noise)

00:03:25.220 --> 00:03:28.251
- How, theoretically,
might time travel via

00:03:28.251 --> 00:03:30.730
wormhole work?

00:03:30.730 --> 00:03:31.670
Whoa!

00:03:31.670 --> 00:03:34.649
- Oh yeah, so, a wormhole enables ...

00:03:34.649 --> 00:03:36.339
By the way if you manage to travel

00:03:36.339 --> 00:03:37.989
some place faster than light,

00:03:37.989 --> 00:03:40.913
you have the capacity to
move backwards in time.

00:03:41.920 --> 00:03:44.450
We've got that one established as well.

00:03:44.450 --> 00:03:47.330
We just don't have any easy way
to travel faster than light.

00:03:47.330 --> 00:03:50.610
But one way that's been
celebrated in science fiction

00:03:50.610 --> 00:03:52.380
and you can write it out on paper

00:03:52.380 --> 00:03:54.120
legitimately, is a wormhole.

00:03:54.120 --> 00:03:57.610
A wormhole, I'm over here
and I wanna get over there

00:03:57.610 --> 00:03:58.830
and I wanna get there quickly.

00:03:58.830 --> 00:04:01.890
I wanna get there before the
end of the commercial break.

00:04:01.890 --> 00:04:05.050
So, you can travel through a wormhole that

00:04:05.050 --> 00:04:07.420
changes the effect of
distance between where you are

00:04:07.420 --> 00:04:09.850
and where you're going,
and then you sort of

00:04:11.130 --> 00:04:12.870
look around when you get
there and you find out,

00:04:12.870 --> 00:04:15.437
Oh my gosh, I've traveled
100,000 light years

00:04:15.437 --> 00:04:17.273
in a matter of a moment.

00:04:18.370 --> 00:04:21.820
When you do that, you
have the capacity to move

00:04:21.820 --> 00:04:25.380
backwards in time,
relative to when you left.

00:04:25.380 --> 00:04:28.130
Now, you don't get to visit yourself.

00:04:28.130 --> 00:04:30.140
You're in a sort of a different

00:04:30.140 --> 00:04:32.690
space-time trajectory.

00:04:32.690 --> 00:04:35.850
So you can't shake hands with
yourself before you left.

00:04:35.850 --> 00:04:37.980
So if that's what you're
thinking of doing, no.

00:04:37.980 --> 00:04:40.503
And by the way, There's a huge paradox

00:04:40.503 --> 00:04:42.680
that people worry about.

00:04:42.680 --> 00:04:44.860
And many people including Steven Hawking,

00:04:44.860 --> 00:04:47.700
the late Steven Hawking,
worry wether this paradox

00:04:47.700 --> 00:04:52.500
would prevent backwards
Time Travel completely.

00:04:52.500 --> 00:04:54.059
Because if you go back in time

00:04:54.059 --> 00:04:56.789
and prevent you parents
from meeting one another,

00:04:56.789 --> 00:04:59.920
then they wouldn't of
ever given birth to you,

00:04:59.920 --> 00:05:03.040
to go back in time to prevent
them from meeting one another.

00:05:03.040 --> 00:05:04.040
- First of all let me just say,

00:05:04.040 --> 00:05:05.810
I stopped listening when you said

00:05:05.810 --> 00:05:07.653
I can't shake hands with myself.

